Now after both availabilities are locked and confirmed, we need to assemble transport leg.

Assemble transport leg action: assemble_transport_leg requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available.

Thus after locking both, we have origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready (from activate actions). We also have origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed (from lock). So we can assemble leg.

After assembling leg, we need to authorize loading: authorize_transport_leg_loading requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized.

Thus we need origin_availability linked to route_task_profile (we have from attach_task_profile). Good.

Now after authorizing loading, we have transport_leg_loading_authorized true.

Now we can mark origin availability dispatch ready: mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready requires origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready. So we can do that.

Similarly mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready requires destination_availability_locked, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready.

Thus after we have both availabilities lock/confirmed and leg assembled+authorized, we can mark both as dispatch ready.

